    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: Unbalanced forces occur when the total forces acting on an object are not
    equal in all directions, causing a change in the object's motion. This can result
    in the object speeding up, slowing down, or changing direction. Unbalanced forces
    are the main cause of acceleration according to Newton's Second Law of Motion.
